{"id":"000VT9","title":"Nate's Killer Lemonade","author":"XeonRisq","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":4,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-31T15:45:36+00:00","posted":"Heute, 16:00 Uhr","rules":"This was inspired by a puzzle concept by SeveNateNine titled \"Productivity Killer (BYOK+)\" , do check this out as it is an amazing idea and execution.\n\nA conversation occurred in discord where I posed the question to Nate if this could be done including all cells; his response was this would be incredibly difficult.\n\nAfter some brainstorming and further discussion, this puzzle was the result, hope you enjoy.\n\n• Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\n• Cages : A cage is a set of orthogonally connected cells which do not contain repeated digits. Cages may not overlap each other. The sum of digits in a given cage is equal to the product of all individual side-lengths of that cage.\n\n(ie: a 1 x 4 cage, is four cells with a sum of 1 x 4 x 1 x 4 = 16)\n\nAll cells must belong to a cage. Only 3 cage shapes may be used (allowing for rotation and reflection)\n\nCircles appear in cages (one circle per cage) and count the total number of cells in that cage.\n\nThe solver will deduce what shape and where the cages exist in the grid.\n• Outside Clues : Clues outside the grid specify the number of cage borders in that row.\n\n• Remote Sums : A digit X in a cage points to a second digit Y located X cells away in its row or column. The number in the top left corner of the cage gives the sum of X+Y.\n\n(denoted by 1 cell cages, these will exist in cages deduced by the solver and will count as one cell)\n\n• SudokuPad link - link to solve puzzle below","solutionCode":"Row 7 followed by Column 4","tags":["Sudoku","Killer (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/7trg6epxp4","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/7trg6epxp4","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":6,"hasSolution":false,"features":["underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-31T15:45:36+00:00"}